From d4f1475c0ecac417b4fe208644a8389259bc3370 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 04:48:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] layout: container queries

Container queries evaluate against each container's content box from the
last layout (query_container_size was todo!()). After layout, if styling
used a container, layout compares the containers' sizes with the previous
layout's and, where one changed, restyles that container's descendants
and lays out once more. Size containers get inline-size containment, so
their intrinsic inline size is that of an empty box. CSSContainerRule
replaces an unimplemented!() that crashed pages reading cssRules (stylo
now parses @container, container units and the container shorthand for
Servo).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
